The flashbang animation of the Light switch
-------------------------------------------
The animation that plays when the mixer page turns light (the grenade that
rolls in, the white flash and the fade) is the work of Silvertree2010,
taken from ApolloOffice:

    https://github.com/Silvertree2010/ApolloOffice  (ui/th.js and three rules
    of ui/index.html, release 0.10.4)

    Written by Silvertree2010
    Licensed under the GNU Affero General Public License, version 3
    (the text is in LICENSE-AGPL-3.0, shipped with every BananaSplit package)

It was ported into BananaSplit on 18 November 2026 (version 2.9.5). It sits
in gui/gui.html, between the lines "---- the flashbang" and "function
applyTheme", and in the style block with the id "flashbang-css". The
timings, the movement and the pixel grenade are his, unchanged. What we
changed: the code is a function of this page (it switches the page's theme
instead of his data-th), the grenade has a longer constant name, and a
second call while one is playing switches at once instead of starting a
second flash.

That part stays under the AGPL-3.0, which the GPL-3.0 allows to be combined
with (section 13 of both licences); the rest of BananaSplit stays
GPL-3.0-or-later. BananaSplit offers its source to everyone who uses it (the
address above), which is what the AGPL asks of a program that people use
over a network (here: the mixer page on your own computer).
